# Node package manager (hub + all submodules)

**Default: bun.** Every Node/TypeScript product installs, runs scripts, and locks
dependencies with `bun` (`bun install`, `bun run <script>`, `bun test`,
`bun.lock` committed). This is the org standard — do not introduce npm or add a
new pnpm project without first trying bun.

**Fallback: pnpm.** Use pnpm only when bun genuinely cannot run the project —
verified incompatibility, not preference: a native addon that only builds
correctly under pnpm/npm's node-gyp flow, a pnpm-workspace-specific feature the
code actually depends on, or a dependency that fails to resolve under bun's
installer after a real attempt. Record *why* in the repo's DEVELOPER.md
(one line: "pnpm — bun install fails on X") so the next person doesn't
re-litigate it.

**Never npm.** No `package-lock.json`, no `npm install`/`npm run` in scripts,
CI, DEVELOPER.md, or Dockerfiles. If a repo still has `package-lock.json`,
that's drift — migrate it (bun first, pnpm only if bun fails) rather than
leaving it.

## Agent checklist

- New Node product: `bun init` / `bun install`, commit `bun.lock`, set
  `"packageManager": "bun@<version>"` in `package.json`.
- Touching an existing npm/pnpm repo: don't silently swap package managers
  mid-unrelated-change — migrate it deliberately (own commit, verify the test
  suite still passes under the new manager) or leave a one-line TODO if it's
  out of scope for the current task.
- CI: use the hub's `lint-test-build-bun.yml` reusable workflow (see
  `docs/agentic-templates/tooling/ci-caller.template.yml`) for bun repos;
  `lint-test-build-node.yml` (pnpm) only for the pnpm-fallback repos.
- Docker: `oven/bun` base image for bun repos, not `node:*` + npm.

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD  — package-lock.json committed, DEVELOPER.md says `npm install`
❌ BAD  — new repo scaffolded with `npm init` "because that's the tsrc default"
❌ BAD  — switched a repo from bun to pnpm because a script felt slower, no real incompatibility

✅ GOOD — bun.lock committed, "packageManager": "bun@1.3.x", DEVELOPER.md says `bun install` / `bun run dev` / `bun test`
✅ GOOD — pnpm-lock.yaml with a one-line DEVELOPER.md note: "pnpm — bun install fails on <native addon X>, see <issue/log>"
```
